# Athlete personal data — never commit to public repo
# (current-state.md files were accidentally force-added 16 May–5 Jul 2026 and
#  publicly served; untracked 5 Jul. Do not re-add athlete files while public.)
ClaudeCoach/athletes/
ClaudeCoach/ironman-analysis/fixtures/
ClaudeCoach/docs-private/

# The rules above cover the athletes/ SUBTREE only. The refresh scripts also write
# athlete data into the ClaudeCoach/ ROOT (refresh-site-data.py -> training-data*.json,
# refresh-public-data.py -> site-data.json), and telegram/history.json sits beside
# the athletes/*/telegram/history.json rule rather than under it. Those root paths
# matched no rule, so all five were tracked in the public repo from May 2026.
ClaudeCoach/training-data.json
ClaudeCoach/training-data-*.json
ClaudeCoach/site-data.json
ClaudeCoach/telegram/history.json
# Same root-vs-subtree gap: the rule above this block is
# ClaudeCoach/athletes/jamie/last_activity_state.json, but activity-watcher.py
# and telegram/bot.py also keep a copy at the ClaudeCoach/ root, which matched
# nothing and was tracked from 8 May 2026.
ClaudeCoach/last_activity_state.json

# ClaudeCoach/public/ is the ONLY athlete-derived directory that is deliberately
# tracked and published. Everything in it is written by lib/public_sanitise.py,
# which copies across an explicit allow-list of fields and refuses the write if a
# forbidden key (weight_kg, hrv, rhr, lthr, injury/pain, notes, ...) appears.
# It is NOT ignored, on purpose: diamondpeak.uk is GitHub Pages built from this
# repo, so anything the dashboards fetch has to be committed here.
#
# Do NOT add a rule for it, and do NOT relax the rules above it. The private
# full-fat files (ClaudeCoach/training-data*.json, ClaudeCoach/site-data.json,
# ClaudeCoach/athletes/**) stay ignored and carry deliberately DIFFERENT
# filenames from their public counterparts, so the two can never be confused:
#   private  ClaudeCoach/training-data-calum.json      (ignored)
#   public   ClaudeCoach/public/training-data-calum.json (tracked, sanitised)

# Untracked 28 Jul 2026 - it was tracked in this PUBLIC repo. The directory rule
# ClaudeCoach/docs-private/ above did not apply because the file was already
# tracked, and a tracked file beats .gitignore.
ClaudeCoach/docs-private/review-checklist.md
.DS_Store
ClaudeCoach/.bug-reviews.json

# Live credentials — never commit to this PUBLIC repo.
# Same root-vs-subtree class of gap as the athlete-data block above: the rules at
# lines 12-15 name config/athletes.json and config/backup.key individually, so
# sibling files in the same directory matched no rule at all. config/ holds
# runtime credentials and encrypted state; nothing in it belongs in a public repo
# unless it is explicitly listed as safe. All of these exist on disk on the VM —
# only the tracking is removed.
# A .gitignore rule alone does NOT prevent this: a tracked path beats .gitignore,
# and `git add -f` walks past it. scripts/check-no-public-secrets.sh is the
# enforcing half and runs on every push to this origin.
ClaudeCoach/config/strava_app.json
ClaudeCoach/config/athletes.json.enc
# Belt and braces for the whole class, not just the files that prompted this.
ClaudeCoach/athletes/*/strava_tokens.json
*.pem
*.env
